        "rationale": "Hatun-ya-chi-sqa expresses caused-to-be-larger result, modifying the whole preliminary-display phrase. It is not an imperative to enlarge the source page or change stored dimensions. The published Chanka visual-description occurrence confirms the participial form, although its immediate topic is caricature/distortion rather than an optical lens; that narrower source meaning is not falsely treated as proof of software magnification. Independent whole-phrase judgment supports enlargement of the presentation itself. The feature-title context permits the configurable magnifier name even when its factor is100percent; it does not assert every current frame is larger.",
